      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "ComfyUI-Pixaroma",
        "ver": "e464839a42e1afed4a568c4be97417ee15091517",
        "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaInfo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Longest Side Pixaroma (2. new size)</b> - Makes the longest side of every picture the size you click, here <b>768</b>. The other side follows, so a tall picture stays tall and nothing is stretched. <b>keep</b> leaves each picture's own shape; the shape chips crop to a square, 16:9 and so on. Small pictures are not made bigger (Allow upscale is off in the gear).</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (3. where and how to save)</b> - Saves the new copies as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/Resized</code>, each with its original name (<code>%input%</code> is the wired file name). Your original pictures are never touched.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Show Text Pixaroma (the names it read)</b> - Shows the names of the pictures it read, one per line, after a Run. It is there so you can see the folder going through.</li><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
